<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="spin-ric-pie" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Spinach-Ricotta Pie</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Crust:</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup unbleached all-purpose flour</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup whole wheat flour</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell><m>\frac{1}{3}</m> cup (<m>5 \frac{1}{3}</m> tablespoons) cold unsalted butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 tablespoons cold buttermilk</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><term>Filling</term></cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>6 ounces baby spinach, roughly chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 small yellow onion, finely chopped</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 tablespoons unsalted butter</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 tablespoons unbleached all-purpose flour</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Kosher salt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Ground white pepper</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>3 large eggs</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 pound ricotta</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup Gruyere, grated</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> cup sour cream or plain yogurt</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Dash freshly grated nutmeg</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon lemon zest</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Sweet paprika</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Combine the white and whole wheat flour. Using 2 knives, cut in the butter. Add the buttermilk.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Pull the dough into a ball. Chill in fridge for 1 hour.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a large skillet, melt the butter over medium heat. Add the onion and cook until limp, about 5 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add the flour and stir to coat the onions. Cook 2 minutes. Add the spinach and cook, stirring, until the spinach is wilted and bright green.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Remove from heat and season with salt and pepper.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a large bowl, beat the eggs. Add ricotta, Gruyere, sour cream, nutmeg and lemon zest. Mix well and set aside.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Roll out chilled dough and place in a 9-inch pie plate.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add the spinach-onion mixture to the ricotta filling. Pour the pie filling into the crust. Smooth with spatula or the back of a large spoon. Sprinkle with paprika.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Bake 45 minutes at <m>375^\circ</m>. Allow pie to rest for 15 minutes before cutting and serving.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          An alternative to the crust above is just to use the <xref ref="reg-crust">Regular Pie Crust</xref> that we use for pies.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>